// The architecture description of ARMv7-M (spec/13-targets.md §13.5): the
// Thumb instruction set of the Cortex-M3 and Cortex-M4 processors without
// the DSP and floating-point extensions.
//
// The description leaves out the IT instruction, so a 16-bit data
// processing instruction always sets the flags, as outside an IT block;
// exceptions, so SVC, BKPT and UDF halt the machine; register operands
// shifted by a constant other than 0; loads and stores with writeback
// other than PUSH, POP and the multiple forms; exclusive accesses,
// coprocessors and the unprivileged forms. The register list of a 16-bit
// LDMIA does not contain its base register. STMIA, LDMIA, STMDB and
// LDMDB write back the base register; STM and LDM do not.
package arch

// ARMv7M describes ARMv7-M.
